{#
  module/Books/view/books/files/files-list-panel.phtml and its list-files.phtml, ported
  as one template.

  The two were separate on the laminas side and are merged here because nothing else
  calls either: `files-list-panel` is rendered from the publication show page alone, and
  `list-files` from `files-list-panel` alone. Splitting a partial that has exactly one
  caller reproduces the indirection without the reuse.

  Expects:
    files        the Drive file rows, each with `url`, `fileName` and optionally
                 `notes`, `size`, `mimeType`, `tags`
    columns      which of those to show, in order
    panel_title  optional; 'Associated Files' when absent, as in the original

  A column name the table does not know is dropped rather than rendered as an empty
  cell — the original `unset()`s it out of the header loop, which silently shortens the
  header while leaving the body loop's `switch` to fall through to its `default`. Here
  the same filtering is applied once, to both.

  These rows come from the Google Drive gateway and never from the database. In the
  capsule the gateway has no credentials, so this panel is empty locally and only the
  empty branch is exercised — worth knowing before concluding that a change here is
  verified.
#}
{% set known = {
    'fileName': 'File name',
    'size':     'Size',
    'tags':     'Tags',
    'notes':    'Notes',
    'mimeType': 'Mime Type',
} %}
{% set shown = columns|filter(c => known[c] is defined) %}
<div class="row"> <!-- row -->
<div class="col-md-12">
<div class="panel panel-default" id="files">
<div class="panel-heading">
    <h3 class="panel-title">{{ translate(panel_title|default('Associated Files')) }}</h3>
</div>
<div class="panel-body">
    {% if files is not empty %}
<div class="responsive-table">
<table class="table"><thead>
<tr>{% for column in shown %}
    <th>{{ translate(known[column]) }}</th>
    {% endfor %}
</tr></thead><tbody>
{% for entity in files %}
<tr>{% for column in shown %}
{%- if column == 'fileName' %}
        <td><a target="_blank" href="{{ entity.url }}">{{ entity.fileName }}</a></td>
{%- elseif column == 'size' %}
        <td>{% if entity.size is defined and entity.size is not null %}{{ file_size(entity.size) }}{% endif %}</td>
{%- else %}
        <td>{{ attribute(entity, column)|default('') }}</td>
{%- endif %}
{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% else %}
<p>{{ translate('No files found.') }}</p>
{% endif %}
</div>
</div> <!-- panel -->
</div> <!-- column 12 -->
</div> <!-- row -->
